1
00:00:00,036 --> 00:00:01,626
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,628 --> 00:00:03,004
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,322 --> 00:00:04,586
(Episode 50)

4
00:00:04,588 --> 00:00:05,993
We're here!

5
00:00:10,541 --> 00:00:11,788
Look at you two.

6
00:00:13,858 --> 00:00:15,827
The newlyweds.

7
00:00:15,828 --> 00:00:18,417
Congratulations. Sa Bin,
you got your wish.

8
00:00:18,611 --> 00:00:19,611
Thank you.

9
00:00:19,782 --> 00:00:22,641
Mom, you did great. Good job.

10
00:00:22,795 --> 00:00:24,481
You two look so good together.

11
00:00:24,715 --> 00:00:26,755
Right? Don't we?

12
00:00:26,757 --> 00:00:28,868
See, Yeong Ju?

13
00:00:29,064 --> 00:00:30,760
I'm so embarrassed. Let's go inside.

14
00:00:30,762 --> 00:00:31,762
Wait.

15
00:00:33,582 --> 00:00:36,895
Thanks to everyone's support,
we had a wonderful honeymoon.

16
00:00:42,788 --> 00:00:45,172
Clear the way. Let's go.

17
00:00:48,175 --> 00:00:49,268
What's wrong?

18
00:00:49,763 --> 00:00:50,763
Mom!

19
00:00:56,442 --> 00:00:57,935
My shoelace came undone.

20
00:01:01,488 --> 00:01:04,259
Mai is traveling around Europe now.

21
00:01:04,262 --> 00:01:06,308
- She's staying at a friend's place.
- You went there?

22
00:01:06,708 --> 00:01:10,323
Sa Bin wanted to visit Mai's place,
so we went to Vietnam.

23
00:01:12,835 --> 00:01:14,548
So she still keeps in touch
with her family.

24
00:01:16,256 --> 00:01:17,548
Come eat.

25
00:01:18,915 --> 00:01:20,682
I missed Korean food so much.

26
00:01:20,848 --> 00:01:23,144
Woo-hoo!

27
00:01:25,124 --> 00:01:26,141
Mom,

28
00:01:26,728 --> 00:01:28,800
was that guy always your type?

29
00:01:28,801 --> 00:01:30,208
No.

30
00:01:31,109 --> 00:01:32,109
But...

31
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:33,628
he's cute.

32
00:01:38,215 --> 00:01:40,628
She said he was cute.

33
00:01:42,415 --> 00:01:44,268
- I'm going out for a bit.
- Where?

34
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:55,628
The kimchi is so good.

35
00:01:56,342 --> 00:01:58,661
It's because Yeong Ju's kimchi
is so good, brother-in-law.

36
00:02:00,576 --> 00:02:01,765
Mom.

37
00:02:02,059 --> 00:02:03,408
What? Should I not call him that?

38
00:02:03,489 --> 00:02:05,571
- He's my brother-in-law.
- Don't.

39
00:02:06,342 --> 00:02:08,970
Hearing you call him that
brings back bad memories.

40
00:02:09,701 --> 00:02:12,522
Okay. I won't.

41
00:02:12,808 --> 00:02:15,922
Sa Bin, it's really
because Yeong Ju's kimchi is so good.

42
00:02:20,581 --> 00:02:21,908
Seung Hyun just stepped out.

43
00:02:27,503 --> 00:02:28,903
I'll do it.

44
00:02:31,348 --> 00:02:32,348
Okay.

45
00:02:48,721 --> 00:02:49,721
What?

46
00:02:51,011 --> 00:02:53,001
Mom, here.

47
00:02:53,468 --> 00:02:54,809
What's all this?

48
00:02:56,768 --> 00:02:58,531
When you get married
and move in with your in-laws,

49
00:02:58,844 --> 00:03:00,379
there are things
you're supposed to bring with you.

50
00:03:00,381 --> 00:03:01,407
Unbelievable.

51
00:03:01,521 --> 00:03:03,167
Did you have all this food prepared
for the in-laws?

52
00:03:04,002 --> 00:03:06,373
The eldest son really comes through.

53
00:03:06,985 --> 00:03:09,105
- Seung Hyun.
- When Mai came,

54
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:12,347
I remembered how impressed you were
by how well she prepared everything,

55
00:03:12,781 --> 00:03:14,048
so I went there and ordered it.

56
00:03:14,168 --> 00:03:15,415
I didn't want you to feel outdone.

57
00:03:15,881 --> 00:03:18,155
I've never done anything like that.

58
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:22,848
I hope your sister-in-law
and your brother like it.

59
00:03:22,857 --> 00:03:24,720
Of course they will.

60
00:03:24,722 --> 00:03:26,648
My sister-in-law is going to cry.

61
00:03:32,642 --> 00:03:34,310
I'm really sorry.

62
00:03:34,768 --> 00:03:36,061
And thank you. Really.

63
00:03:38,289 --> 00:03:39,635
As long as you're happy.

64
00:03:42,715 --> 00:03:44,480
They say no younger brother
can compare to his older brother.

65
00:03:44,481 --> 00:03:46,869
Seung Hyun, why do that alone?
You should've told me.

66
00:03:47,584 --> 00:03:49,089
You said you would benefit
from having an older brother.

67
00:03:49,563 --> 00:03:50,675
That's true.

68
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:52,428
Nice. You're taking care of everything.

69
00:03:56,728 --> 00:04:00,844
Even when I'm gone,
treat Se Ri and Ji Ni as you do now.

70
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:04,865
Living here with them without you...

71
00:04:05,472 --> 00:04:06,472
doesn't feel right.

72
00:04:08,001 --> 00:04:09,999
- I think the same.
- Then what are we supposed to do?

73
00:04:10,055 --> 00:04:11,635
They have nowhere else to go.

74
00:04:12,348 --> 00:04:15,753
And seeing Se Ri make my dress...

75
00:04:16,021 --> 00:04:17,568
made me think about a lot of things.

76
00:04:18,095 --> 00:04:20,033
I really thought
that even if the sky fell,

77
00:04:20,187 --> 00:04:23,039
I'd never see Se Ri again.

78
00:04:23,821 --> 00:04:26,448
I even cursed Ji Ni so many times.

79
00:04:26,948 --> 00:04:28,301
We did too.

80
00:04:29,515 --> 00:04:30,953
And yet that same girl...

81
00:04:31,287 --> 00:04:32,807
helped O Reum in his sickness...

82
00:04:33,208 --> 00:04:34,922
and helped me with my proposal.

83
00:04:35,557 --> 00:04:37,868
I don't think family is just about blood.

84
00:04:39,042 --> 00:04:40,362
You're too kind.

85
00:04:40,881 --> 00:04:41,940
And Ji Ni...

86
00:04:42,309 --> 00:04:44,394
isn't she actually pretty nice
once you get to know her?

87
00:04:44,541 --> 00:04:45,951
I like her.

88
00:04:46,673 --> 00:04:47,948
Get along with her.

89
00:04:49,195 --> 00:04:50,195
And you,

90
00:04:51,925 --> 00:04:54,547
you must never forget
what she did for O Reum.

91
00:04:55,082 --> 00:04:56,706
- Okay.
- Ji Ni,

92
00:04:56,714 --> 00:04:58,748
the more I see her,
the less I understand her.

93
00:04:58,914 --> 00:05:00,068
The way she treats us...

94
00:05:00,069 --> 00:05:02,707
seems different from how
she treats her friends outside.

95
00:05:02,813 --> 00:05:03,813
What are you talking about?

96
00:05:05,421 --> 00:05:07,228
- I'm not sure, but...
- Then don't say it.

97
00:05:08,035 --> 00:05:09,695
You're shutting me down
without even hearing me out?

98
00:05:09,697 --> 00:05:12,460
Yeah. You're too bossy with Seung Woo.

99
00:05:12,462 --> 00:05:13,977
He's over thirty now.

100
00:05:15,135 --> 00:05:16,135
Are you upset?

101
00:05:16,995 --> 00:05:18,240
Forget it. I don't know.

102
00:05:19,827 --> 00:05:21,634
Go. Don't worry about us.

103
00:05:21,948 --> 00:05:22,948
Okay.

104
00:05:23,795 --> 00:05:25,075
Listen to your brother.

105
00:05:26,141 --> 00:05:27,695
You take care of yourself, Yeong Ju.

106
00:05:27,795 --> 00:05:29,901
Half my worries are about you.

107
00:05:29,922 --> 00:05:31,128
Stop calling her Yeong Ju.

108
00:05:31,242 --> 00:05:33,399
Calling her Yeong Ju in front of Sa Bin...

109
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:35,175
looks bad. Don't do it.

110
00:05:35,982 --> 00:05:37,568
- I was just...
- Yeah.

111
00:05:37,909 --> 00:05:40,238
It's a little inappropriate. He's right.

112
00:05:42,206 --> 00:05:44,422
Okay, Mom.

113
00:05:51,901 --> 00:05:53,984
Now that you're here,
I can leave without worrying.

114
00:05:54,572 --> 00:05:55,572
Yeah.

115
00:06:00,562 --> 00:06:01,641
That's not fair.

116
00:06:08,575 --> 00:06:09,735
I'll put it in the car.

117
00:06:13,901 --> 00:06:15,539
I'm counting on you here.

118
00:06:16,166 --> 00:06:17,181
Don't worry.

119
00:06:17,441 --> 00:06:19,545
I'll treat it like my own home.

120
00:06:20,319 --> 00:06:21,319
Yeong Ju...

121
00:06:23,622 --> 00:06:25,694
Mom, take care.

122
00:06:26,429 --> 00:06:27,528
You have to be happy.

123
00:06:27,968 --> 00:06:29,455
If you're uncomfortable, come right back.

124
00:06:29,607 --> 00:06:30,877
I'll take care of everything.

125
00:06:31,371 --> 00:06:33,247
Don't worry. That won't happen.

126
00:06:33,708 --> 00:06:35,649
Ma'am, be happy.

127
00:06:38,302 --> 00:06:39,302
Thank you.

128
00:06:44,628 --> 00:06:46,218
You gave me the courage to do this.

129
00:06:46,732 --> 00:06:47,732
See you again.

130
00:07:07,015 --> 00:07:08,698
Yeong Ju, don't cry.

131
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:09,788
You'll ruin your makeup.

132
00:07:10,842 --> 00:07:12,621
Leave things here to me and go.

133
00:07:12,675 --> 00:07:14,122
I'm most worried about you.

134
00:07:15,135 --> 00:07:16,328
Please take care of her.

135
00:07:16,549 --> 00:07:18,106
Yes. Don't worry.

136
00:07:20,961 --> 00:07:22,582
If you're leaving, go on.

137
00:07:22,755 --> 00:07:25,259
Those going to work,
get going too. Come on.

138
00:07:25,261 --> 00:07:26,334
We're going.

139
00:07:27,968 --> 00:07:29,006
Take care.

140
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:32,499
You look beautiful, Yeong Ju.
You look great!

141
00:08:06,695 --> 00:08:07,695
Yeong Ju.

142
00:08:08,255 --> 00:08:09,748
She's really gone.

143
00:08:17,455 --> 00:08:18,455
Right.

144
00:08:30,308 --> 00:08:31,308
Where did she put it?

145
00:08:32,589 --> 00:08:33,589
Where did she put it?

146
00:08:35,061 --> 00:08:36,541
Did she move it somewhere else?

147
00:08:39,755 --> 00:08:43,015
Could Seung Hyun have put it away?

148
00:08:59,891 --> 00:09:01,030
Seriously.

149
00:09:18,188 --> 00:09:19,188
That's it, right?

150
00:09:20,768 --> 00:09:22,995
She wouldn't have hidden it
in Seung Woo's room.

151
00:09:23,775 --> 00:09:26,341
Looks like she took it with her.

152
00:09:27,588 --> 00:09:28,772
I should've taken it then.

153
00:09:46,922 --> 00:09:48,048
You're back already?

154
00:09:48,701 --> 00:09:49,714
It's close.

155
00:09:49,982 --> 00:09:51,275
I just dropped her off.

156
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:52,674
Right.

157
00:09:53,282 --> 00:09:54,722
We'll clean our own rooms.

158
00:09:54,724 --> 00:09:56,600
I just want to do it for you.

159
00:09:56,602 --> 00:09:57,602
It's okay.

160
00:10:10,907 --> 00:10:13,060
You haven't even had a proper vacation
in a while.

161
00:10:13,662 --> 00:10:16,557
So spend some time with your son...

162
00:10:16,736 --> 00:10:17,886
and get plenty of rest.

163
00:10:17,888 --> 00:10:21,315
Yeong Ju isn't used to running
the household here.

164
00:10:21,422 --> 00:10:22,521
I should stay and help...

165
00:10:22,523 --> 00:10:24,672
That's why we're going to be alone.

166
00:10:25,555 --> 00:10:27,191
We'd be more uncomfortable if you stayed.

167
00:10:27,193 --> 00:10:28,208
Still...

168
00:10:29,695 --> 00:10:32,881
We moved in together
so we could get to know each other better.

169
00:10:34,408 --> 00:10:35,621
Give us some privacy.

170
00:10:37,442 --> 00:10:38,701
That's right, Su Yeon.

171
00:10:40,195 --> 00:10:41,301
Since my wife...

172
00:10:41,402 --> 00:10:44,214
wants to spend time with an old schoolmate
who's also her sister-in-law,

173
00:10:44,216 --> 00:10:46,035
- please understand.
- Okay.

174
00:10:46,875 --> 00:10:48,939
Ma'am, you're incredible.

175
00:10:48,941 --> 00:10:50,935
I don't think I could do that.

176
00:10:51,335 --> 00:10:55,584
If my friend married the brother-in-law
I used to pack lunches for,

177
00:10:55,586 --> 00:10:57,941
- I can't even imagine it.
- Come on.

178
00:10:58,475 --> 00:11:01,841
If he's happy, what more reason do I need?

179
00:11:01,895 --> 00:11:05,655
Still, you used to be the queen
of this house, with three men around you.

180
00:11:05,657 --> 00:11:07,061
It can't be helped.

181
00:11:08,155 --> 00:11:09,268
Anyway, have a good trip.

182
00:11:16,475 --> 00:11:19,395
Yeong Ju, the wedding food looks so good.

183
00:11:19,722 --> 00:11:21,902
Yeong Ju's eldest son prepared everything
in advance.

184
00:11:21,942 --> 00:11:23,648
I was so touched.

185
00:11:24,155 --> 00:11:25,953
Tell her sons to come by too.

186
00:11:25,955 --> 00:11:27,921
They'll want to see
how their mom is living.

187
00:11:27,975 --> 00:11:29,814
- Is that okay, Joong Bin?
- Of course.

188
00:11:30,535 --> 00:11:31,535
Honey.

189
00:11:31,849 --> 00:11:34,048
Go ahead. Why are you looking at me?

190
00:11:34,915 --> 00:11:37,338
You did a great job raising your children.

191
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:39,541
No, they still have a lot to learn.

192
00:11:41,041 --> 00:11:42,958
We should greet your brother.

193
00:11:43,038 --> 00:11:44,841
That's right.
We should greet you, Joong Bin.

194
00:11:44,881 --> 00:11:46,453
There's no need. We're brothers.

195
00:11:46,522 --> 00:11:48,400
- It's okay.
- Honey.

196
00:11:48,402 --> 00:11:49,735
You can't do that.

197
00:11:50,108 --> 00:11:52,340
We skipped the traditional ceremony
because we had a small wedding.

198
00:11:52,935 --> 00:11:55,208
Should we? Okay.

199
00:12:05,322 --> 00:12:06,381
Thank you.

200
00:12:06,882 --> 00:12:09,268
Yeong Ju, please take good care of Sa Bin.

201
00:12:10,008 --> 00:12:13,077
He may be getting older,
but he's still a kid at heart.

202
00:12:13,466 --> 00:12:15,065
Joong Bin, seriously.

203
00:12:15,295 --> 00:12:18,301
There's quite an age gap between us,
and we lost our parents early.

204
00:12:18,695 --> 00:12:20,271
I said I'd be a proper older brother,

205
00:12:20,273 --> 00:12:22,013
but my job kept me away from home,

206
00:12:22,088 --> 00:12:24,448
so he had to go through a lot in my place.

207
00:12:25,182 --> 00:12:27,637
Now that things have turned out this way,
let's...

208
00:12:27,638 --> 00:12:29,321
Why are you making such a long speech?

209
00:12:29,442 --> 00:12:32,149
Yeong Ju, let's get along from now on.

210
00:12:32,590 --> 00:12:34,988
Yes, Sun Kyung. Please show me the ropes.

211
00:12:36,022 --> 00:12:38,415
I love hearing you talk like that.

212
00:12:38,502 --> 00:12:41,761
Who would've thought
we'd have such a happy occasion this year?

213
00:12:47,561 --> 00:12:48,561
Ta-da!

214
00:12:50,782 --> 00:12:52,882
Was the room always this big?

215
00:12:53,821 --> 00:12:55,295
When I came before...

216
00:12:55,395 --> 00:12:56,846
Joong Bin had it redecorated.

217
00:12:56,848 --> 00:12:57,852
Do you like it?

218
00:12:58,946 --> 00:13:00,055
I love it.

219
00:13:04,022 --> 00:13:06,742
I still can't believe it,
even looking at the pictures.

220
00:13:07,016 --> 00:13:08,016
Me neither.

221
00:13:10,555 --> 00:13:12,328
I can't believe it
even when I'm holding you like this.

222
00:13:13,542 --> 00:13:15,128
Come sit here for a moment.

223
00:13:18,688 --> 00:13:19,688
Let me...

224
00:13:20,222 --> 00:13:21,538
give you a massage.

225
00:13:21,852 --> 00:13:23,838
No, we should go downstairs.

226
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,268
Just a moment.

227
00:13:27,385 --> 00:13:30,602
I'll do the laundry from our trip too.

228
00:13:30,709 --> 00:13:31,882
You're going to do the laundry?

229
00:13:32,275 --> 00:13:34,322
No way. Just leave it.

230
00:13:34,368 --> 00:13:36,148
- Just leave yourself alone, Yeong Ju.
- What?

231
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:38,668
I mean, stay right there on the bed.

232
00:13:38,982 --> 00:13:40,681
Don't get up.

233
00:13:43,842 --> 00:13:46,574
We're living with your brother
and his wife now.

234
00:13:46,722 --> 00:13:48,518
You can't be saying
all these lovey-dovey things.

235
00:13:48,786 --> 00:13:50,341
I can say whatever I want.

236
00:13:56,691 --> 00:13:58,504
Sa Bin, what's that?

237
00:13:58,908 --> 00:14:00,777
The laundry from our trip.

238
00:14:00,975 --> 00:14:02,764
Today's my last day off,
so I have to do it now.

239
00:14:02,942 --> 00:14:05,248
Why are you doing that?

240
00:14:05,601 --> 00:14:06,676
Then who will?

241
00:14:07,449 --> 00:14:08,962
I heard Su Yeon went to Jeju Island too.

242
00:14:10,011 --> 00:14:11,279
Would you like to do it for me?

243
00:14:11,448 --> 00:14:13,978
That's not what I meant.

244
00:14:14,003 --> 00:14:16,815
Yeong Ju's too tired.

245
00:14:17,448 --> 00:14:20,543
She's spent her whole life raising kids,
taking care of her in-laws,

246
00:14:20,862 --> 00:14:23,177
and running a singing class.
She worked herself to the bone.

247
00:14:23,202 --> 00:14:24,339
You know that better than anyone.

248
00:14:25,408 --> 00:14:27,852
You've had it easy all this time,

249
00:14:27,933 --> 00:14:30,009
but from now on,
she deserves an easy life.

250
00:14:30,561 --> 00:14:33,426
I'm not going to let her do a thing.

251
00:14:38,010 --> 00:14:39,225
Let's have dinner early.

252
00:14:39,227 --> 00:14:41,290
I only had noodles for lunch.
I'm starving.

253
00:14:42,801 --> 00:14:45,754
- What's with that outfit?
- This?

254
00:14:45,992 --> 00:14:47,582
Sa Bin bought it for me.

255
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:49,088
- I like it.
- Take it off. Now.

256
00:14:50,427 --> 00:14:51,600
That Ji Hu!

257
00:14:52,358 --> 00:14:53,993
I told him to come home early!

258
00:14:54,967 --> 00:14:56,637
How could he come home early?

259
00:14:56,801 --> 00:14:59,245
He's busy getting the publishing company
back up and running.

260
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,191
(Ho Chi Minh City)

261
00:15:02,313 --> 00:15:04,001
Hello. Thank you.

262
00:15:08,401 --> 00:15:09,401
Ji Ni.

263
00:15:09,688 --> 00:15:12,631
Pages eight through twelve.
Are these your drawings?

264
00:15:12,810 --> 00:15:13,871
Hold on.

265
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:16,750
No, they're not.

266
00:15:17,117 --> 00:15:18,143
Those?

267
00:15:18,582 --> 00:15:19,836
Do Hee drew those.

268
00:15:20,667 --> 00:15:21,740
Do Do Hee?

269
00:15:23,828 --> 00:15:25,745
You must've had a lot of meetings.
They're really good.

270
00:15:25,770 --> 00:15:27,661
Right? That's what I'm wondering too.

271
00:15:27,774 --> 00:15:30,840
She doesn't even know if they're
a brother and sister or two sisters,

272
00:15:30,953 --> 00:15:32,397
yet she drew them beautifully.

273
00:15:32,577 --> 00:15:34,516
Maybe she really is a genius.

274
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:36,902
If that's really true,

275
00:15:37,385 --> 00:15:38,420
she could be.

276
00:15:38,452 --> 00:15:40,159
Could you redraw these, Ji Ni?

277
00:15:40,842 --> 00:15:42,808
The tone is different
from your previous work.

278
00:15:44,118 --> 00:15:45,729
Sure. I'll redraw them.

279
00:15:46,855 --> 00:15:49,260
But in the original story,
the Sun and Moon...

280
00:15:49,284 --> 00:15:52,803
escape the tiger by grabbing a rope
that comes down from the sky.

281
00:15:53,170 --> 00:15:56,341
But I love that in our version,
they fight back against the tiger.

282
00:15:56,402 --> 00:15:57,561
Whose idea was that?

283
00:15:57,803 --> 00:15:58,847
Ji Ni's.

284
00:15:58,969 --> 00:16:01,078
She's quite the fighter.

285
00:16:01,365 --> 00:16:02,592
No, I'm not.

286
00:16:02,617 --> 00:16:04,748
I'm hardly some kind of fighter.

287
00:16:05,802 --> 00:16:07,291
You're lying too, Ji Ni.

288
00:16:07,315 --> 00:16:09,433
- We all saw it.
- When?

289
00:16:09,642 --> 00:16:11,395
When we went to the Van Gogh exhibition.

290
00:16:11,667 --> 00:16:13,897
You landed a flying kick on that guy
who was beating up his girlfriend.

291
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:17,954
The amazing part was
she only used her feet.

292
00:16:17,972 --> 00:16:20,015
When I started training,
I promised my mom...

293
00:16:20,047 --> 00:16:22,345
- I'd never hurt my hands.
- So that's why.

294
00:16:23,055 --> 00:16:24,835
I was worried you'd hurt your hands too.

295
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:26,348
You looked like a warrior princess.

296
00:16:28,048 --> 00:16:30,860
Were all of you there that day?

297
00:16:32,068 --> 00:16:33,068
We saw it firsthand!

298
00:16:33,373 --> 00:16:35,074
Don't even think about denying it.

299
00:16:36,208 --> 00:16:38,264
"So I'm the only one who missed it."

300
00:16:38,628 --> 00:16:39,943
I'd like to say that,

301
00:16:40,358 --> 00:16:42,921
but I saw it too.
You're quite the fighter.

302
00:16:43,314 --> 00:16:45,182
- When?
- Back then.

303
00:16:45,206 --> 00:16:47,360
There was that time you trashed
the cafe with Do Hee,

304
00:16:47,548 --> 00:16:49,819
and when you took on those thugs
who went after that guy with the bad leg.

305
00:16:49,826 --> 00:16:51,578
- And...
- That's enough.

306
00:16:51,603 --> 00:16:53,226
You don't have to list them all.

307
00:16:53,705 --> 00:16:55,065
It's hot.

308
00:16:55,463 --> 00:16:57,782
So when did you start training?

309
00:16:57,807 --> 00:17:01,126
I didn't go to high school.
I went to a martial arts gym to train.

310
00:17:02,321 --> 00:17:04,829
I think the reason
women's stories keep falling apart...

311
00:17:05,087 --> 00:17:08,502
is that they rely on others
to keep them safe.

312
00:17:08,922 --> 00:17:11,865
But we live in a society
where we can't survive without others.

313
00:17:12,165 --> 00:17:14,728
The Sun and Moon help each other.

314
00:17:14,922 --> 00:17:17,112
And when it's time to fight,
you have to fight.

315
00:17:17,481 --> 00:17:19,910
- There shouldn't be...
- One-sided salvation.

316
00:17:19,935 --> 00:17:21,722
They save each other.

317
00:17:22,073 --> 00:17:24,430
So it's a fresh take on the folktale?

318
00:17:24,921 --> 00:17:26,730
We'll make that the focus
of the marketing too.

319
00:17:33,648 --> 00:17:35,408
But you said you have a fiancé.

320
00:17:35,426 --> 00:17:36,675
When are you getting married?

321
00:17:36,699 --> 00:17:39,145
He's seeing someone else these days.

322
00:17:39,622 --> 00:17:41,072
And it's my friend.

323
00:17:45,568 --> 00:17:50,778
But I don't think you'd
let someone steal your boyfriend.

324
00:17:51,402 --> 00:17:53,257
Still, that must hurt.

325
00:17:53,348 --> 00:17:54,565
I'm going to cry.

326
00:17:54,822 --> 00:17:57,865
Actually, I was always jealous of her
back in school.

327
00:17:58,235 --> 00:18:00,078
Her dad is something else.

328
00:18:00,522 --> 00:18:02,693
He goes all out for his daughter.

329
00:18:03,229 --> 00:18:06,143
I only became friends with her
because I was jealous of her dad.

330
00:18:06,737 --> 00:18:09,367
That's so sad, right?

331
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:12,792
Right? I'm lonely.

332
00:18:13,762 --> 00:18:17,109
So keep me company today.
Let's meet, grab a bite, and hang out.

333
00:18:17,256 --> 00:18:18,256
Will you?

334
00:18:18,522 --> 00:18:20,361
I'll buy you dinner.

335
00:18:21,522 --> 00:18:22,743
Hey, she's just like you.

336
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:24,885
You were always begging people
to hang out with you too.

337
00:18:24,909 --> 00:18:26,000
The director?

338
00:18:26,882 --> 00:18:28,480
No way.

339
00:18:28,505 --> 00:18:31,720
Ever since he joined the company,
he's been begging people to hang out.

340
00:18:33,030 --> 00:18:34,363
Hey!

341
00:18:35,082 --> 00:18:36,876
He may seem prickly,

342
00:18:37,226 --> 00:18:39,302
but deep down,
he'll do whatever he's asked.

343
00:18:39,375 --> 00:18:40,987
And he's so affectionate.

344
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:45,076
You're totally my type.

345
00:18:45,278 --> 00:18:46,465
You should go.

346
00:18:46,564 --> 00:18:47,865
We're having a meeting.

347
00:18:48,158 --> 00:18:49,902
Why? I can join you.

348
00:18:52,559 --> 00:18:53,680
Let's do it together.

349
00:19:05,116 --> 00:19:07,409
You're good. Better than store-bought.

350
00:19:07,434 --> 00:19:08,609
I'm going to sell them too.

351
00:19:08,885 --> 00:19:10,817
Really? Are you opening a restaurant?

352
00:19:11,058 --> 00:19:12,624
A food truck.

353
00:19:15,602 --> 00:19:17,789
Are you going to drive around
looking for Mai?

354
00:19:18,655 --> 00:19:20,217
Selling banh xeo?

355
00:19:22,762 --> 00:19:24,920
You're more of a romantic than you look.

356
00:19:25,349 --> 00:19:28,450
Well, if you're anything like your dad,
you'd be a romantic.

357
00:19:34,495 --> 00:19:37,676
Love is about playing favorites.

358
00:19:37,694 --> 00:19:40,619
If you love everyone, that's just
love for humanity. Is that really love?

359
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:43,812
And your mom has remarried,

360
00:19:44,086 --> 00:19:45,965
so it's time to let it go.

361
00:19:46,468 --> 00:19:47,984
Does being right mean
you can say anything?

362
00:19:48,608 --> 00:19:50,547
You should also think about how
the other person feels.

363
00:19:51,817 --> 00:19:53,393
You're right.

364
00:20:01,775 --> 00:20:02,775
This is good.

365
00:20:07,175 --> 00:20:09,309
Seung Hyun!

366
00:20:13,315 --> 00:20:14,358
What are you doing?

367
00:20:14,522 --> 00:20:17,667
Move this vanity to the storage room.

368
00:20:17,955 --> 00:20:20,375
I'm going to use my vanity here.
Your mom said it's okay.

369
00:20:25,955 --> 00:20:28,800
Are you keeping this picture here too?

370
00:20:28,824 --> 00:20:30,618
Yeah.

371
00:20:30,620 --> 00:20:32,436
I always kept it on my vanity.

372
00:20:33,526 --> 00:20:34,640
Don't move into this room.

373
00:20:34,665 --> 00:20:36,985
You can stay in the annex, or...

374
00:20:37,536 --> 00:20:39,449
I'd rather you
find your own place and move out.

375
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,696
Because of this picture?

376
00:20:41,698 --> 00:20:43,780
Having his picture
in the master bedroom...

377
00:20:43,820 --> 00:20:45,510
is simply not an option for us.

378
00:20:46,376 --> 00:20:49,176
- You're so difficult.
- Right back at you.

379
00:20:49,278 --> 00:20:50,428
We're both the same.

380
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:05,490
Let's go home. I'll drive you.

381
00:21:05,492 --> 00:21:07,204
No, I'm stopping by the bookstore.

382
00:21:07,346 --> 00:21:09,428
- Then come with me. I'll drive you.
- No, I'll take a cab.

383
00:21:09,497 --> 00:21:10,497
Why?

384
00:21:11,024 --> 00:21:12,112
Am I making you uncomfortable?

385
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:15,732
Better safe than sorry.

386
00:21:17,015 --> 00:21:19,487
Let's just focus on work
so no one gets the wrong idea.

387
00:21:21,368 --> 00:21:22,368
Ji Ni.

388
00:21:23,428 --> 00:21:24,535
You haven't left yet?

389
00:21:24,940 --> 00:21:26,576
- Want a ride?
- Sure.

390
00:21:26,608 --> 00:21:27,838
Drop me off at the bookstore.

391
00:21:28,393 --> 00:21:29,393
See you tomorrow.

392
00:21:31,641 --> 00:21:35,114
- Spicy rice cakes before the bookstore?
- Sure.

393
00:21:35,139 --> 00:21:37,315
- Let's get something spicy.
- Yes! I love spicy food.

394
00:21:53,507 --> 00:21:55,895
Give it to me.

395
00:21:55,983 --> 00:21:57,962
No, let me carry it inside for you.

396
00:21:57,986 --> 00:21:59,409
No, I'm fine. Give it to me.

397
00:21:59,434 --> 00:22:01,305
It's okay. This is really heavy.

398
00:22:01,307 --> 00:22:03,358
I said I'm fine. Come on.

399
00:22:03,547 --> 00:22:06,746
Thank you, sir.

400
00:22:07,033 --> 00:22:08,326
Seriously!

401
00:22:13,649 --> 00:22:14,649
Honey, take this.

402
00:22:15,936 --> 00:22:17,740
What's all this?

403
00:22:17,742 --> 00:22:18,983
When did you go out?

404
00:22:19,008 --> 00:22:22,466
I told you the kids are coming over today.

405
00:22:22,882 --> 00:22:25,017
I went out to find some fresh seafood.

406
00:22:25,042 --> 00:22:27,878
You went to the fish market
yourself this early in the morning?

407
00:22:27,986 --> 00:22:29,650
Why are you so surprised?

408
00:22:30,135 --> 00:22:32,036
I told you I'd get along with her.

409
00:22:40,975 --> 00:22:42,553
Looks fresh.

410
00:22:43,250 --> 00:22:44,250
Honey!

411
00:23:09,559 --> 00:23:10,559
What are you doing?

412
00:23:13,262 --> 00:23:17,398
I brought my dishes over
when I brought Yeong Ju's dress.

413
00:23:17,547 --> 00:23:19,973
I thought I'd switch things up
for a change.

414
00:23:20,385 --> 00:23:22,184
It's a shame
to leave them sitting in storage.

415
00:23:22,670 --> 00:23:24,270
Don't.

416
00:23:25,441 --> 00:23:27,727
- Again with "don't"?
- Just leave it.

417
00:23:27,875 --> 00:23:30,837
If you want to change things around,
do it somewhere else.

418
00:23:31,521 --> 00:23:33,474
I'm going to keep things
the way my mom had them.

419
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:36,813
But she told me to make myself at home!

420
00:23:37,033 --> 00:23:40,258
And fine, I understand the picture.

421
00:23:40,381 --> 00:23:44,257
Honestly, he's gone,
and she has remarried,

422
00:23:44,281 --> 00:23:46,381
so I said I understood,
even though I didn't.

423
00:23:46,715 --> 00:23:48,777
But this is going too far.

424
00:23:48,802 --> 00:23:50,322
Why do you have a problem
with everything I do?

425
00:23:50,347 --> 00:23:51,586
Just don't.

426
00:23:56,834 --> 00:23:57,942
Seriously!

427
00:24:04,468 --> 00:24:06,093
Yeong Ju!

428
00:24:06,279 --> 00:24:08,137
Yeong Ju, I'm losing my mind.

429
00:24:08,155 --> 00:24:10,556
You told me to make myself at home.

430
00:24:10,714 --> 00:24:12,925
But then you told Seung Hyun...

431
00:24:12,949 --> 00:24:15,710
to make my life miserable at every turn?

432
00:24:15,735 --> 00:24:18,210
Are you trying
to drive me out of the house?

433
00:24:18,498 --> 00:24:20,748
Do you really think I'll leave quietly?

434
00:24:21,547 --> 00:24:24,225
What do you mean, "quietly?"
I can't hear you.

435
00:24:30,124 --> 00:24:33,541
Who's making whose life miserable here?
You keep saying you're being mistreated.

436
00:24:33,746 --> 00:24:35,931
Do whatever you want. I'm busy.

437
00:25:01,276 --> 00:25:04,674
Fine. Come at me one more time.

438
00:25:06,481 --> 00:25:09,288
I'll tear this whole house apart.

439
00:25:23,936 --> 00:25:25,297
She really did all this?

440
00:25:33,552 --> 00:25:36,467
She really went all out.

441
00:25:36,491 --> 00:25:38,166
Yeong Ju!

442
00:25:38,728 --> 00:25:39,763
Sun Kyung.

443
00:25:41,013 --> 00:25:42,013
I'm dizzy.

444
00:25:42,822 --> 00:25:44,266
Didn't you overdo it?

445
00:25:44,648 --> 00:25:46,630
I had to.

446
00:25:47,262 --> 00:25:50,537
It's Yeong Ju's first time
having her family over.

447
00:25:50,562 --> 00:25:51,913
But where's Yeong Ju?

448
00:25:52,264 --> 00:25:53,572
I don't know.

449
00:25:53,673 --> 00:25:57,161
Don't push yourself too hard.

450
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:12,640
Yeong...

451
00:26:21,775 --> 00:26:23,029
Yeong Ju.

452
00:26:23,519 --> 00:26:24,855
Yeong Ju.

453
00:26:25,380 --> 00:26:26,602
Yeong Ju.

454
00:26:28,409 --> 00:26:29,581
Sa Bin.

455
00:26:30,456 --> 00:26:31,494
When did you get here?

456
00:26:31,623 --> 00:26:33,314
You must be exhausted.

457
00:26:33,762 --> 00:26:36,278
Sun Kyung cooked everything herself,

458
00:26:36,537 --> 00:26:38,426
and she's about to collapse.

459
00:26:38,450 --> 00:26:40,669
It would've been nice if you'd helped.

460
00:26:40,774 --> 00:26:43,488
Seung Hyun and Seung Woo are coming too.

461
00:26:44,608 --> 00:26:45,652
What did you say?

462
00:26:49,659 --> 00:26:53,183
You don't have to rush...

463
00:26:56,734 --> 00:26:59,001
- Sun Kyung.
- You're here.

464
00:27:00,282 --> 00:27:02,767
The kids will love all this, right?

465
00:27:03,633 --> 00:27:05,006
They'll love it.

466
00:27:05,031 --> 00:27:08,836
This is fried, this is steamed,
and this is soup...

467
00:27:09,042 --> 00:27:11,063
You really went all out, Sun Kyung.

468
00:27:11,088 --> 00:27:13,480
I won't forget what you've done for us.

469
00:27:13,481 --> 00:27:15,005
You don't owe me anything.

470
00:27:18,222 --> 00:27:19,369
Looks like they're here.

471
00:27:25,208 --> 00:27:27,617
Go greet them. The kids are here.

472
00:27:28,660 --> 00:27:29,660
Go ahead.

473
00:27:59,126 --> 00:28:02,485
(Family Register)

474
00:28:02,509 --> 00:28:04,467
Everyone will see what you're really like.

475
00:28:04,492 --> 00:28:05,509
What am I really like?

476
00:28:05,534 --> 00:28:07,881
Those two are always together.
How could I not suspect something?

477
00:28:07,883 --> 00:28:08,977
I heard she broke up because of you.

478
00:28:09,002 --> 00:28:10,735
Isn't it weird that he's with you
in the middle of the night?

479
00:28:10,759 --> 00:28:12,917
- Stop. Take it out. Now.
- Cha Seung Hyun!

480
00:28:12,942 --> 00:28:15,222
Come at me one more time,
and I'll sell this house and leave.

481
00:28:15,247 --> 00:28:17,326
You said you'd repay your debt to O Reum.

482
00:28:17,351 --> 00:28:19,002
You've really got some nerve.

483
00:28:19,027 --> 00:28:20,110
Go through it again.

484
00:28:20,135 --> 00:28:22,517
You'll reflect and realize,
"I really shouldn't have been born."

485
00:28:22,518 --> 00:28:24,465
Dad, please help me.

486
00:28:25,858 --> 00:28:27,858
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
